Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`  
  – `station_id`: join key to match a trip’s start / end station with a station record  
  – `status`: identify whether a station is “active” (only keep active stations)  
  – `council_district`: district number used for grouping and counting  

• `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips`  
  – `start_station_id`: starting station for a trip (join to stations)  
  – `end_station_id`: ending station for a trip (join to stations)  

Main conditions that will be applied  

1. Keep only stations whose `status = 'active'`.  
2. Join each trip to both its start and end station to obtain two council‑district codes.  
3. Keep trips where the start and end council districts are the same.  
4. Exclude trips whose `start_station_id = end_station_id`.  
5. Count trips per council district and take the district with the highest count.  

Ten exploratory / step‑by‑step SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows)  

```sql
-- 1. Distinct station statuses
SELECT DISTINCT status
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Sample of stations that are active
SELECT station_id, name, council_district, status
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations`
WHERE status = 'active'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Sample of trips with their start station & time
SELECT trip_id, start_station_id, end_station_id, start_time
FROM `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Join a trip to its start station’s district
SELECT t.trip_id,
       t.start_station_id,
       s.council_district AS start_district
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s
  ON   t.start_station_id = s.station_id
WHERE  s.status = 'active'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Join a trip to both start and end stations (active only)
SELECT t.trip_id,
       t.start_station_id,
       t.end_station_id,
       s1.council_district AS start_district,
       s2.council_district AS end_district
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s1
  ON   t.start_station_id = s1.station_id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s2
  ON   t.end_station_id   = s2.station_id
WHERE  s1.status = 'active'
  AND  s2.status = 'active'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Trips that start and end in the same district but different stations
SELECT t.trip_id,
       s1.council_district AS district,
       t.start_station_id,
       t.end_station_id
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s1
  ON   t.start_station_id = s1.station_id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s2
  ON   t.end_station_id   = s2.station_id
WHERE  s1.status = 'active'
  AND  s2.status = 'active'
  AND  s1.council_district = s2.council_district
  AND  t.start_station_id <> t.end_station_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Count of such trips per council district
SELECT s1.council_district AS district,
       COUNT(*) AS same_district_diff_station_trips
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s1
  ON   t.start_station_id = s1.station_id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s2
  ON   t.end_station_id   = s2.station_id
WHERE  s1.status = 'active'
  AND  s2.status = 'active'
  AND  s1.council_district = s2.council_district
  AND  t.start_station_id <> t.end_station_id
GROUP  BY district
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Same as #7 but ordered by count descending
SELECT s1.council_district AS district,
       COUNT(*) AS trip_count
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s1
  ON   t.start_station_id = s1.station_id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s2
  ON   t.end_station_id   = s2.station_id
WHERE  s1.status = 'active'
  AND  s2.status = 'active'
  AND  s1.council_district = s2.council_district
  AND  t.start_station_id <> t.end_station_id
GROUP  BY district
ORDER  BY trip_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Retrieve just the top‑1 district by trip count
SELECT s1.council_district AS district,
       COUNT(*) AS trip_count
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s1
  ON   t.start_station_id = s1.station_id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s2
  ON   t.end_station_id   = s2.station_id
WHERE  s1.status = 'active'
  AND  s2.status = 'active'
  AND  s1.council_district = s2.council_district
  AND  t.start_station_id <> t.end_station_id
GROUP  BY district
ORDER  BY trip_count DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 10. (Same as #9, presented as the final answer query)
-- Description: returns the numeric council district with the highest number of
-- bike trips that start and end inside the same active district but at
-- different stations.
SELECT s1.council_district AS highest_trip_district
FROM   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_trips` AS t
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s1
  ON   t.start_station_id = s1.station_id
JOIN   `bigquery-public-data.austin_bikeshare.bikeshare_stations` AS s2
  ON   t.end_station_id   = s2.station_id
WHERE  s1.status = 'active'
  AND  s2.status = 'active'
  AND  s1.council_district = s2.council_district
  AND  t.start_station_id <> t.end_station_id
GROUP  BY highest_trip_district
ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
LIMIT 1;
```
